<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tutul Xiu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Xiu dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tutul Xiu were a Maya ruling lineage of northern Yucatán, associated with Uxmal and, after the fall of Mayapán in the mid-15th century, with the town of Maní. Their rulers, the halach uinic, governed a province of many towns. In 1542 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ah-kukum-xiu">Ah Kukum Xiu</a> submitted to the Spanish, and the family kept noble status and genealogical records under colonial rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tutul-xiu.jpg" alt="Tutul Xiu" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cacicazgos_mayas.jpg: Jaontiveros Mexico_States_blank_map.svg: Sémhur derivative work: ecelan (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cacicazgos_mayas_-_es.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
